# Build context for service/Dockerfile. The image build only needs the Gradle
# project and the sources it compiles; everything else must never enter the
# context or the build cache.
#
# Two rules govern this file. It must cover every path the Dockerfile does *not*
# COPY, and it must cover every kind of file that can carry a secret, a local
# vault, a database, a log, or a tool cache — because anything left in the
# context is also sent to the daemon and kept in a build layer. `./gradlew
# checkContainerContract` asserts the second rule mechanically, so adding a tool
# or a state directory to the repository without adding it here fails the build
# rather than silently shipping it.

# Version control and CI
.git
**/.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.pijul
**/.pijul
.pijulignore
.ignore
.ci

# Gradle, Kotlin, and build output
.kotlin
**/.kotlin
.gradle
**/.gradle
**/build
build-logic/.gradle
**/out
**/sdk-drift
**/*.g
**/.gradletasknamecache

# Documentation, contracts, and generated SDKs are not compiled into the image
docs
CONTRIBUTING.md
SECURITY.md
README.md
CODEOWNERS

# Local developer state and secrets
.editorconfig
.idea
**/.idea
.vscode
**/.vscode
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
*.code-workspace
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
*.lcov
htmlcov
**/htmlcov
**/reports
.pytest_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.mypy_cache
**/.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
**/.ruff_cache
.tox
**/.tox
**/*.egg-info
**/.eggs
**/dist
.venv
.venv-*
.python-sdk-venv
**/.venv
**/node_modules
**/target
**/.cache
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# Runtime and vault state
**/*.db
**/*.db-*
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite-*
**/*.sock
**/*.sock.lock
**/.tanseki
**/logs
**/*.log
**/hs_err_pid*
**/replay_pid*
